/T (At the same time, India has called for greater accountability from developed nations in fulfilling their commitments under the Paris Agreement \(Narain, 2021\). By highlighting the principle of "common but differentiated responsibilities," India ensures that climate action is pursued in a manner that recognizes historical inequities and supports the needs of vulnerable populations \(Sengupta, 2020\).)
